## Trust boundary and evidence

Named assumptions are the supplied MPY semantics for the modeled Python
constructs, K's reachability implementation, the Haskell/LLVM backends, integer
hooks, and the SMT solver. All formal claims depend on those components. There
is no unproved program-defined helper or opaque value primitive.

