These tests support intent and implementation adequacy; they are not the
universal proof.

## Excluded behavior

Negative integers, non-integer elements, mutation of the input list, and
behavior outside the supplied MPY subset are outside the formal domain.
Termination is not part of the partial-correctness theorem, although concrete
finite-list executions terminate. CPython equivalence beyond the relevant
modeled constructs is assumed rather than proved.
